      "min_spread": 0.005,
      "n": 1,
      "note": "Primary corner-liveness guard for this bench: VREF at the nominal supply must move by at least 5 mV across the 15-point process/temperature matrix. It spans ~33 mV (1.1747 V at the hot corners to 1.2082 V at the cold ones), so this is a wide-margin assertion that the .lib corner include and .temp really are reaching the simulator. It is placed on VREF rather than on the line shift because VREF is the quantity with a large, well-understood corner dependence; the line shift is a second-order effect measured in tens of microvolts and is a poor liveness signal.",
